    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="process-timeline">
          
          <div class="process-step">
            <div class="process-step__icon">1</div>
            <h2>Initial Phone Consultation</h2>
            <p>When you reach out, we'll discuss your pet's condition and answer any immediate questions. We'll handle the scheduling and administrative details over the phone so that the actual visit can remain entirely focused on your pet.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="process-step">
            <div class="process-step__icon">2</div>
            <h2>Arrival at Your Home</h2>
            <p>The veterinarian will arrive quietly and give your pet time to get comfortable. We never rush. We will find the most comfortable spot, whether that is on their favorite bed, a sunlit rug, or even outside in a peaceful yard.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="process-step">
            <div class="process-step__icon">3</div>
            <h2>Gentle Sedation</h2>
            <p>We administer a mild sedative that allows your pet to fall into a deep, peaceful sleep. This ensures they are completely relaxed and unaware of any discomfort before the final procedure begins. This usually takes 5 to 15 minutes.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="process-step">
            <div class="process-step__icon">4</div>
            <h2>The Final Goodbye</h2>
            <p>Once your pet is in a deep sleep and you have had all the time you need, the veterinarian will administer the final injection. It is quiet, painless, and feels like drifting deeper into sleep. You can hold them or lay beside them throughout.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="process-step">
            <div class="process-step__icon">5</div>
            <h2>Respectful Aftercare</h2>
            <p>If you have chosen cremation services, we will respectfully transport your pet. We handle every companion with the same care we would give our own pets. If you prefer home burial, we will help you prepare for that transition.</p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

